    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The town’s name comes from an Aboriginal term meaning “one who cooks with stones,” reflecting its long traditional meeting area.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        23,
        24,
        25
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://assiniboia.net/visit_us/history.html"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "During the Great Depression, officials hired unemployed men to build the town’s sewer system, a project completed in 1948.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        9,
        10
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Assiniboia%2C_Saskatchewan"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Assiniboia Regional Park, founded in 1977, spans three locations around town and offers a 9‑hole golf course and a boat‑launch lake with walleye and perch.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2,
        12,
        14
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Assiniboia%2C_Saskatchewan"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "From 1942 to 1944, the town’s airfield served as an elementary flight school during World War II.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        11
